  "findings": [
    "Original EN891/KO783 guide lines and EN166/KO166 quiz lines fully read; all20questions retained, corrected and aligned.",
    "Pinned Calico3.32.2/operator1.42.6; distinguishes Calico Kubernetes1.34–36 tested range from EKS standard1.34–36/extended1.31–33 and upstream1.37. Removed fabricated historical minimum/LTS compatibility tables.",
    "Separated AWS native policy from Calico installation and corrected automatic EKS add-on update claim; native standard support started in VPC CNI1.14, not EKS1.14. Current VPC CNI1.21+ admin ClusterNetworkPolicy included without equating it with Calico tiers.",
    "Added required ANNOTATE_POD_IP and additive Pod-patch RBAC verification; preserve existing add-on values with actual jq-tested candidate, handle null/empty JSON values, reject malformed/YAML inputs until explicitly converted. Do not leave AWS policy startup mode when its agent is absent or use toggling as a migration procedure.",
    "Fixed real Helm keys/API server OSS availability and separate CRDs; removed unsupported Typha replicas/top-level FelixConfiguration/flow-log fields and nodeMetadata credential claim. One installation owner and CRD migration limits explicit.",
    "Fargate native/Calico policy exclusions, AutoMode alternate-plugin ban and node-local DNS, Hybrid AWS-maintained Cilium build support, Windows HNS boundaries added. Full CNI is separate from native-policy disable and requires control-plane/webhook reachability planning.",
    "Removed broad unnecessary calico-node IAM policy; identity belongs to actual AWS-calling components. SG-for-Pods Calico requires standard mode/VPC CNI1.11+; branch ENI and node-SNAT security-group behavior documented.",
    "Original EN duplicate destination mapping discarded backend selector. Replaced with single namespace-scoped selector+port mapping, explicit TCP/UDP resolver destinations and same-namespace gateway prerequisite; no cluster-wide default deny or ALB-as-Pod-label assumption.",
    "Current official EKS rollback supports previous minor within7days after eligible in-place upgrade; add-ons/Calico not automatically reverted. Removed unconditional older-operator rollback and destructive node cleanup recipes.",
    "Prefix delegation uses env values, not invented ConfigMap keys; IP targets override warm prefix target. Removed ungrounded component dollar prices/sysctl/resource-limit and production-ready guarantees. eBPF kept as separate documented procedure with both kube-proxy coexistence settings and DSR limits.",
    "All10figures actually viewed;4retained with corrected captions,6references removed for Felix packet-path/drop-return, obsolete product comparison and AWS control-plane boundary/Typha sizing errors. Source assets and foreign prose untouched.",
    "Followup2026-09-12:AWSgeneralalternate-CNIpage stillstatescoreCalico/CiliumsupportforHybrid; specializedHybridCNIpage listsAWSmaintainedCilium/movesCalicoexamples. Qualified prior wording: do notinferCalicosupportterminationfromexamplemove;exactdistribution/capabilitysupportrequiresconfirmation.4currentVuecompilationspass;no code changed."
  ],
